{"type":"standard","title":"Jay Feely","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jay Feely</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3807503","titles":{"canonical":"Jay_Feely","normalized":"Jay Feely","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jay Feely</span></span>"},"pageid":1126535,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Jay_Feely_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/330px-Jay_Feely_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":421},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0f/Jay_Feely_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2808,"height":3584},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377212804","tid":"2687a4a4-bb1f-11f1-a2f2-8ad63de45e4a","timestamp":"2026-09-28T09:29:49Z","description":"American football player and sportscaster (born 1976)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Feely","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Feely?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Feely?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jay_Feely"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Feely","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jay_Feely","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Feely?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jay_Feely"}},"extract":"Thomas James Feely is an American former professional football player. He started his playing career as a placekicker with the Florida Bobcats in the Arena Football League (AFL) as a free agent in 1999 before playing for several National Football League (NFL) teams. Following his retirement until 2025, Feely worked as a reporter and analyst for the NFL on CBS.","extract_html":"<p><b>Thomas James Feely</b> is an American former professional football player. He started his playing career as a placekicker with the Florida Bobcats in the Arena Football League (AFL) as a free agent in 1999 before playing for several National Football League (NFL) teams. Following his retirement until 2025, Feely worked as a reporter and analyst for the NFL on CBS.</p>"}